{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/431772-2ed-bale-hounds","id":431772,"title":"2ed Bale Hounds","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-07T14:29:35-08:00","id":431772,"title":"2ed Bale Hounds","content":"So as most of you know, I started my <b>Werewolf</b> game last year as 1.5(?) ed-ish chronicle set in Northern Sweden about Bale Hounds pack in small town on outskirts of civilization. PCs are newly made Forsaken pack that want's to free humans from the slavery to the Maeljin's pawns. Thing is - we want to close the story, and as I see the difference in the 2ed are not so much from what we done to this date - I would want to change game to proper 2ed, with small pause we have in sessions. And so the Bale Hounds NPCs pack as final confrontation approaches - I need new stats for them.<br /> <br /> But, as we all know, Bale Hounds were cut out of 2ed corebook - they are not even mentioned in Maeljin sidebar. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> When I come to the Character Creation section, I saw changes with Blood and Bone or the Touchstones - and it got me some questions on to how relate them to the 2ed Bale Hounds, at least for now, as fan material. Here they are:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Bale Hounds are all about working for Maeljins as seeding their &quot;sin&quot; in the world around them. In 1ed it was nice as character could just pickup Vice from Seven Deadly Sin and she get the Willpower from the making work for it's master. It was Win-Win situation. But in 2ed we have Blood&amp;Bone system, and connecting it to the Lords of Sins is not that easy. Maybe Bale Hounds choose other source of taking back Willpowers? Like <i>Vice-Ridden</i> (**) Merit from the <b>God Machine Rules Update</b>? Would then character could get back more than one Willpower point if he could fullfill then both Vice and Bone in once scene, for example?</li> <li>Bale Hounds, in 1ed, were very low Harmony wolves. But in 2ed, lower strata of Harmony means you are more spirits oriented - does this mean Bale Hounds could have middle or even higher starta of Harmony, doing what they do in game? How is then Sin-Eating the Souless Wolf needed for them?</li> <li>Connecting to second subtopic - very low Harmony ( 3 and lower ) means character does not gain advantage from the Physical Touchstones. Could still character have them, even if they are for now lower? I ask, as could be cool scene generator pointing close ones or important places of Bale Hounds NPCs as possible targets for the PCs pack, and the weakness in enemies to explore. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></li> </ol>More questions to come soon... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-07-2015, 05:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T14:33:22-08:00","id":431793,"title":"","content":"I doubt Soulless Wolf's Sin Eating is necessary now. <br /> <br /> I suspect Bale Hounds will be primarily low-Harmony because many of the vicious behaviors they engage in are Spirit breaking points. Some might be high or balanced, though, and that could get interesting ...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T14:00:42-07:00","id":433094,"title":"","content":"Other question - <b>If Blood Talons can declare Siskur-Dah on Bale Hounds, can they declare it on the PCs?</b> Does Bale Hounds should work as new Tribe, or rather single cultists that were once part of previous Tribes? ( And with that some ex-Blood Talon could invoke Siskur-Dah on the PCs pack then ).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T14:27:15-07:00","id":433120,"title":"","content":"On your latter question, not sure what you mean - werewolves certainly can declare a Sacred Hunt on player characters, and they don't need to be Blood Talons to do so.<br /> <br /> If there isn't a Blood Talon as ritemaster, of course, then the Siskur-Dah benefits will be less relevant for the hunt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T14:35:44-07:00","id":433124,"title":"","content":"Any Ritemaster can declare the sacred hunt on just about anything or anyone. They don't gain the sacred prey benefits if the target isn't their preferred prey, but they can still call the hunt. <br /> <br /> If Bale Hounds, Pure, or rival packs want to call the hunt on the players' characters, they are free to do so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T14:39:13-07:00","id":433126,"title":"","content":"Huh. I wonder if the Bale Hounds have a sacred prey, and if so what it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T14:49:51-07:00","id":433161,"title":"","content":"@Vice: How about giving them a Vice as part of being a Bale Hound? They have Blood and Bone as normal, but also a human Vice. This should also make them eligible for getting Vice-ridden.<br /> <br /> @Being low Harmony would seem to make them poor agents of the Maelijin (with their difficulty interacting with the world of flesh)... tricky question...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T14:58:25-07:00","id":433184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/431772-2ed-bale-hounds?p=433161#post433161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Vice: How about giving them a Vice as part of being a Bale Hound? They have Blood and Bone as normal, but also a human Vice. This should also make them eligible for getting Vice-ridden.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, that right there's a motive to join the Hounds-the Maeljin offer humanity along with the changes that are part of an Uratha's nature.<br /> <br /> It's kind of a dark part of humanity that most humans would be glad to be without, but it's humanity...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T15:26:41-07:00","id":433224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/431772-2ed-bale-hounds?p=433184#post433184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, that right there's a motive to join the Hounds-the Maeljin offer humanity along with the changes that are part of an Uratha's nature.<br /> <br /> It's kind of a dark part of humanity that most humans would be glad to be without, but it's humanity...</div> </div> </div> </div>And that in turn would mean high (as in fleshy) Harmony. Checks out!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T16:41:22-07:00","id":433270,"title":"","content":"Them being a 9th tribe is more likely with this new harmony set up, and I think soulless wolf can still have a roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T16:52:58-07:00","id":433279,"title":"","content":"I had though the Pure would have the Unworthy, the Weak, and the Unbeliever as their sacred prey. I liked the idea of them having a descriptor they could arbitrarily tack on to anyone while still fitting in with their themes.<br /> <br /> But the Bale Hounds always seemed more about corruption, than killing. Not that the Pure aren't. It's possible their 'hunt' would be a theological one. More about conversion, than capture.. Their victory is either a new convert, or a dead one. Sometimes they're more interested in being proponents of sin, getting a Forsaken to give in just once is a win. My only issue with that would be if it was handled weakly the Bale Hounds might come across as more of a reaffirmation of a werewolf's own faith rather than an appreciable alternative. 'Join the dark side!' 'No.' And now the Forsaken feels inspired. If you wanted them to hunt people or things, the Virtuous might fit, allowing them to take down spirits, werewolves, and humans and the in-betweens.<br /> <br /> It'll be interesting to see what's done with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-08-2015, 07:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T17:50:21-07:00","id":433339,"title":"","content":"I say they hunt Power.<br /> <br /> Which is to say, they hunt anyone who gets in the way of their desires, or that prey whose death furthers those desires.<br /> <br /> That can be converting a disciple too...as well as faking normal tribe allegiance, they can reasonably insinuate themselves into packs by hunting one of the more conventional tribe targets...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T18:35:48-07:00","id":433380,"title":"","content":"I also hope they keep the alternative types of Bale Hounds. Maybe not all three but I like the idea that while there may be an entire tribe or lodge, there's also the occasional Forsaken, Pure or Ghost Wolf who made a deal at one point and has to stick to it. I could see that having a presence in game as an Aspiration, so that when the Maeljin sends word for you to do something, in exchange for what they did for you, that Aspiration lingers, taking up one of your aspiration slots because it's hard to dwell on other things until you're off the hook. They may not consider themselves Bale Hounds but the Maeljin have a hook in their heart and mind, no matter how small, and it cannot be denied.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T00:22:00-07:00","id":433643,"title":"","content":"Lodge of the lake.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T00:40:59-07:00","id":433646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/431772-2ed-bale-hounds?p=433279#post433279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had though the Pure would have the Unworthy, the Weak, and the Unbeliever as their sacred prey. I liked the idea of them having a descriptor they could arbitrarily tack on to anyone while still fitting in with their themes.<br /> <br /> But the Bale Hounds always seemed more about corruption, than killing. Not that the Pure aren't. It's possible their 'hunt' would be a theological one. More about conversion, than capture.. Their victory is either a new convert, or a dead one. Sometimes they're more interested in being proponents of sin, getting a Forsaken to give in just once is a win. My only issue with that would be if it was handled weakly the Bale Hounds might come across as more of a reaffirmation of a werewolf's own faith rather than an appreciable alternative. 'Join the dark side!' 'No.' And now the Forsaken feels inspired. If you wanted them to hunt people or things, the Virtuous might fit, allowing them to take down spirits, werewolves, and humans and the in-betweens.<br /> <br /> It'll be interesting to see what's done with them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have the Bale Hounds have complete control over the Rage. They can enter into it just fine and exit out of it with complete and utter control. Even under pain of death, they do not Rage. They can be in Gauru without having to roll. They spread the lie that they've achieved perfection.<br /> <br /> That's because the Maeljin hold the reigns. When they tug, the Bale Hounds fly right into Death Rage. No rolls, no chances to resist. When the Maeljin tug, they tug hard, ripping apart whatever the Bale Hounds decides to hold dear. Whatever scrap of virtue they can salvage. They are not the kings to the Rage but rather slaves to it.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T00:41:07-07:00","id":433647,"title":"","content":"We cut the handful of references to Bale Hounds from the book, as it was better to not mention them at all than give them two sentances here and there. One of those was, indeed, in the Wounds description, where it said that as well as tainting spirits, the mysterious okay-it's-the-Inferno-but-we-aren't-calling-it-that world beyond the Wounds sometimes tainted the People, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T01:38:21-07:00","id":433667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/431772-2ed-bale-hounds?p=433647#post433647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We cut the handful of references to Bale Hounds from the book, as it was better to not mention them at all than give them two sentances here and there. One of those was, indeed, in the Wounds description, where it said that as well as tainting spirits, the mysterious okay-it's-the-Inferno-but-we-aren't-calling-it-that world beyond the Wounds sometimes tainted the People, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>But they are mentioned. Page 232 and 264.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T09:56:54-07:00","id":434166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Felipe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/431772-2ed-bale-hounds?p=433667#post433667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But they are mentioned. Page 232 and 264.</div> </div> </div> </div>And this why they should be mentioned in Maeljin Sidebar. They will pop-up randomly in the line. Better is to say &quot;there are werewolves working for the Lords of the Wounds&quot; than then do not have them officially in corebook, but then have them in gameline mentioned time qnd time again...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-09-2015, 04:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T11:54:46-07:00","id":434344,"title":"","content":"It would be easier to just remove them from the advance pdf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T13:24:20-07:00","id":434462,"title":"","content":"I maybe weird, but I'm not get it. In 1ed Bale Hounds were mentioned in corebook and later developed in to full splat. In 2ed they are not in corebook, but still there are plans for them to return. I ask - why? If Bale Hounds are part of 2ed gameline ( and I hope they are ), they should be mentioned in few ( <i>literally</i> few ) words in sidebar - then dedicated fan want to find them - they look for them in 1ed books. Their full write-up for 2ed <b>still</b> be needed - just they could show up in materials that are done now, or fans can buy 1ed books. And they still will need 2ed mechanics for them.<br /> <br /> So why not at least put them in this famous Maeljin sidebar? Once in the whole corebook, like Maelijins they work for? We still do not have Maeljins servants spirits and Wounds very accurate description so the supplement is still highly needed. Maeljins are mentioned once in book, why not mention once their werewolf servants?<br /> <br /> And when we mentioned Bale Hounds in corebook, the gameline will be cohesive with 1ed - and, as pointed, with settings in 2ed. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-09-2015, 04:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T10:42:54-07:00","id":435933,"title":"","content":"You have word count and theme drift to worry about if you are the developer. Better to have a focused core experience than a generalized one, including Bale Hounds means devoting pages to a concept not everyone uses (or uses sparingly.) I can easily see why they were left out and I'm expecting that they'll get their own book or a major section of an antagonists book sometime down the road. The Bale Hounds are a holdover from Apocalypse's Black Spirals and I'd like Forsaken to further develop it's own identity. I would have greatly preferred that they and the Maeljin were the focus of 2nd ed, they aren't so all we can do is voice support for a project that adds them later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T11:02:16-07:00","id":435969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/431772-2ed-bale-hounds?p=435933#post435933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Bale Hounds are a holdover from Apocalypse's Black Spirals and I'd like Forsaken to further develop it's own identity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never saw much similarity there, but I don't know that much about the Black Spiral wolves. It just seems like the current Maeljin and the Wyrm aren't really the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T11:09:14-07:00","id":435977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/431772-2ed-bale-hounds?p=435933#post435933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You have word count and theme drift to worry about if you are the developer. Better to have a focused core experience than a generalized one, including Bale Hounds means <b>devoting pages to a concept not everyone uses (or uses sparingly.)</b> I can easily see why they were left out and I'm expecting that they'll get their own book or a major section of an antagonists book sometime down the road. The Bale Hounds are a holdover from Apocalypse's Black Spirals and I'd like Forsaken to further develop it's own identity. I would have greatly preferred that they and the Maeljin were the focus of 2nd ed, they aren't so all we can do is voice support for a project that adds them later.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then why did we get 5 idigam, of which each took up 4~5 pages, and who are, by nature, something you'll use <i>one</i> of in your chronicle, if that. I have no real sympathy for arguments of &quot;we didn't have space&quot; when you spent <i>37 pages</i> on the Idigam. You could've gotten away with one, you know, as an example, and then released the others later in another sourcebook.<br /> <br /> Then you'd have a whole 12~15 more pages to play with! And we could have had the Lamprey Hosts, and Bale Hounds, and...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T11:20:37-07:00","id":435990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/431772-2ed-bale-hounds?p=435933#post435933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You have word count and theme drift to worry about if you are the developer. Better to have a focused core experience than a generalized one, including Bale Hounds means devoting pages to a concept not everyone uses (or uses sparingly.) I can easily see why they were left out and I'm expecting that they'll get their own book or a major section of an antagonists book sometime down the road.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I mean about using 4-5 <b>words</b> extra in the sidebar, to mark their existence in gameline -<i> not</i> 4-5 pages of their write up in corebook...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T11:21:23-07:00","id":435993,"title":"","content":"The book was initially going to be the Idigam Chronicles, they were the antagonist the book focused on since the initial stages of developement. What should they have done? Drop all the 32 leftover pages in a garbage bag and keep one sample Idigam and expand the rest of the antagonists? Too late I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T11:34:39-07:00","id":436004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/431772-2ed-bale-hounds?p=435990#post435990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And I mean about using 4-5 <b>words</b> extra in the sidebar, to mark their existence in gameline -<i> not</i> 4-5 pages of their write up in corebook...</div> </div> </div> </div>Man, wordcount is a thing, they may not have those 4-5 words <i>at all</i>. From where would you cut those, then? Because that's how it works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T11:49:25-07:00","id":436019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/431772-2ed-bale-hounds?p=435977#post435977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then why did we get 5 idigam, of which each took up 4~5 pages, and who are, by nature, something you'll use <i>one</i> of in your chronicle, if that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which vary dramatically in outlook and ability, may wind up opposing each other, and <i>had the fucking title card before this was officially a second edition.</i><br /> <br /> Precedent and story hooks matter, man. I've gotten a better idea of how things work in the WoD from character examples and other fluff than I have from a blind reading of the mechanics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I have no real sympathy for arguments of &quot;we didn't have space&quot; when you spent <i>37 pages</i> on the Idigam. You could've gotten away with one, you know, as an example, and then released the others later in another sourcebook. </div> </div> </div>And instead we get the central story-catalyst out-of-context problems their own section just like the Strix did in Requiem 2e and we can safely give the Maeljin and the Bale Hounds (who come with their own baggage that hooks into a part of the cosmology with an entire 1e book dedicated to it) pagespace in a book that isn't already crammed full of stuff \u2014 you'll recall that one of the issues commonly mentioned in 1e was the glut of antagonists and that 2e now has the added weight of five different focal antagonists to the degree that <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/425614-petition-for-tribes-of-the-moon-2e-working-title\">there's a proposal to use that division for partial tribe-books</a>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Then you'd have a whole 12~15 more pages to play with! And we could have had the Lamprey Hosts, and Bale Hounds, and... </div> </div> </div>I can't tell if you're acting childish as an ironic thing here or if you actually don't understand how distribution of focus operates in a written work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T12:28:00-07:00","id":436051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/431772-2ed-bale-hounds?p=436004#post436004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Man, wordcount is a thing, they may not have those 4-5 words <i>at all</i>. From where would you cut those, then? Because that's how it works.</div> </div> </div> </div>[Going to the 2ed corebook PDF][Looking on the <i>Maeljin</i> sidebar in question on the page 76]<br /> <br /> Maybe I'm blind, but I easily see one extra spare line over the sidebar - enough to add &quot;They even corrupted some Uratha, called Bale Hounds.&quot; on 11 line of text - 7 words, looking on sidebar it's exactly one line that is extra space on this particular page.<br /> <br /> There, I saved the Bale Hounds in 2ed corebook in the way that's totally enough for them now. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T12:33:20-07:00","id":436054,"title":"","content":"That assumes in second edition Bale Hounds are corrupted by the Maeljin, and not members of the Ninth Tribe under Viruhk-Ur.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T12:47:47-07:00","id":436061,"title":"","content":"No father, you aren't seeing the similarity because there isn't much of one beyond &quot;bad morally wrong wolves&quot;. It's Bout the same as comparing garou to forsaken.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T13:01:51-07:00","id":436077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/431772-2ed-bale-hounds?p=436051#post436051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[Going to the 2ed corebook PDF][Looking on the <i>Maeljin</i> sidebar in question on the page 76]<br /> <br /> Maybe I'm blind, but I easily see one extra spare line over the sidebar - enough to add &quot;They even corrupted some Uratha, called Bale Hounds.&quot; on 11 line of text - 7 words, looking on sidebar it's exactly one line that is extra space on this particular page.<br /> <br /> There, I saved the Bale Hounds in 2ed corebook in the way that's totally enough for them now. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's not how it work. You really are just kidding now, right? I could stuff maybe 6 more paragraphs vertically on the margins, that would do nothing to the fact that if you have a x-thousand wordcount and you already wrote x-thousand words you have to cut something to add something.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T13:10:46-07:00","id":436086,"title":"","content":"May as well do outside the box thinking. Hell I posted (I assume) and unpopular topic about a potential update for the hounds. The minimal mention we might get is no where near as useful to us as looking at blasphemies and trying to update that would be. Turn the tAinted moon gifts into facets would be a far better boom then a brief nothing mention in a side bar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T13:55:08-07:00","id":436203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/431772-2ed-bale-hounds?p=436077#post436077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's not how it work. You really are just kidding now, right? I could stuff maybe 6 more paragraphs vertically on the margins, that would do nothing to the fact that if you have a x-thousand wordcount and you already wrote x-thousand words you have to cut something to add something.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>No, I did not kidding with adding 7 words to the text where they can fit and will make sense in later reading of gameline - where servants of Thing A described in 1ed corebook, are not mentioned in sidebar about Thing A of 2ed, where those servants are one of possible large corruption way of PCs. No need for whole margins of text. No need for extra pages. Just adding 7 words and move a text on the free space bar above.<br /> <br /> Hell, the Errata topic have larger individual alteration to the corebook text even.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/431772-2ed-bale-hounds?p=436086#post436086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">May as well do outside the box thinking. Hell I posted (I assume) and unpopular topic about a potential update for the hounds. The minimal mention we might get is no where near as useful to us as looking at blasphemies and trying to update that would be. Turn the tAinted moon gifts into facets would be a far better boom then a brief nothing mention in a side bar.</div> </div> </div> </div>My point is that both new players and new STs should know Bale Hounds <b>exists</b> in setting. They should be pointed in corebook, that if we mention Maeljins, the werewolf that works for them are a thing. If new players will buy 2ed material and they will see ad &quot;Bale Hounds antagonists&quot;, they should not scratch their heads on this &quot;totally new thing&quot;, only they should want to know about them from the corebook. If I'm for proper Bale Hounds splat write up in supplements? Hell, yeah! But I'm also on marking that Bale Hounds exists and pointing then new players to look for the old 1ed matieral - that Onyx Path still sell, as I know it - and sate their thirst for dark knowledge of Maeljins <b>before</b> the 2ed supplement will comes up.<br /> <br /> Come on, guys, if we mentioning Maeljins in corebook, should not werewolf that work for them ( and what group PCs can become ) also be mentioned in the same book? Not described. not having full splat. But at least mentioned in one line of text?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-10-2015, 05:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T14:21:21-07:00","id":436259,"title":"","content":"I think it's entirely a stylistic choice, and it's up to the developer whether he wants to even broach the subject if he doesn't feel he has the space to do it properly. Same reason why the Brood was cut from B&amp;S.<br /> <br /> I also don't think it matters that much at all.<br /> <br /> (Also, I know people have criticized both Promethean and Mummy for having cores that functionally go &quot;hey, these exist but we can't tell you about them&quot;. Granted, that was in a paragraph or more instead of a blink-and-you'll-miss-it reference, but still.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T15:03:10-07:00","id":436315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/431772-2ed-bale-hounds?p=436019#post436019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which vary dramatically in outlook and ability, may wind up opposing each other, and <i>had the fucking title card before this was officially a second edition.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>I am aware of these facts, yes. This is why my post was more joking and less &quot;OMG ONYX PATH YOU ARE INCOMPETENT AND SHOULDN'T BE ALLOWED TO WRITE STUFF&quot;, which is not my opinion in the least.<br /> <br /> I did, however, forget that the writing had already been well underway when they changed it over when it became a Second Edition; I will apologize for that (my question is whether or not they had those 32 pages written up at that point, though; did they post the tentative outline for the book at any point, or has that only been done for Hurt Locker and Changeling 2e?).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Precedent and story hooks matter, man. I've gotten a better idea of how things work in the WoD from character examples and other fluff than I have from a blind reading of the mechanics. </div> </div> </div>To be honest? I agree. <i>In most cases</i>. Which is why my &quot;ideal&quot; arrangement of the topic would have been a step-by-step &quot;here is how you take your Idigam from an idea to something you can <i>hunt</i>&quot;, with maybe one or two other examples. The mini ideas they had, the Idigam that coalesced in a junkyard with Influences of Fire and Rust and Sharpness, or the Earthbound who could not harm goatherds? That <i>fired my imagination</i>. The ones we got full write-ups for just felt... eh? I'm trying not to insult the writers here, but the full write-ups took me from going AWW YEAH IDIGAM to &quot;I could care less about these guys. I want to hear more about the other Prey, please.&quot;<br /> <br /> (To be fair, that was also my initial reaction to the Strix. I wanted to be reading more about Vampires, not Shadow Owls. So who knows, maybe the Idigam will grow on me?)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And instead we get the central story-catalyst out-of-context problems their own section just like the Strix did in Requiem 2e and we can safely give the Maeljin and the Bale Hounds (who come with their own baggage that hooks into a part of the cosmology with an entire 1e book dedicated to it) pagespace in a book that isn't already crammed full of stuff \u2014 you'll recall that one of the issues commonly mentioned in 1e was the glut of antagonists and that 2e now has the added weight of five different focal antagonists to the degree that <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/425614-petition-for-tribes-of-the-moon-2e-working-title\">there's a proposal to use that division for partial tribe-books</a>. </div> </div> </div>As I mentioned in another thread, B&amp;S could get away with that because Strix were one of four things, while the Idigam are trying to be one of eight things (eleven things, if you count the extra stuff that they can make as separate things). Plus, pulling in other gamelines with a very different distribution of &quot;baddies&quot; is kinda... not entirely comparing apples to apples.<br /> <br /> Idigam just feel like their own thing, and I'm not sure how I would use them to fuel stories without having one <i>right there</i>. I mean, with Strix or the God-Machine or Angels or whatever, you can play on dread and paranoia and the like; you can bluff that they are coming and make it work.<br /> <br /> But Werewolf? Werewolf isn't about being <i>afraid</i> of things. It's about a lot of things (the hunt, family, territory, coming to terms with how you changed and are changing), but it isn't about worrying about nebulous threats. You've got that Pure pack next door baring their fangs at you, the Beshilu making trouble down by the docks, and some spirits getting too big for their britches on YOUR territory... so why should you care about some nebulous threat?<br /> <br /> Oh sure, they might hate you particularly, or are insults to the memory of Father/Mother Wolf... but how is that different than your normal prey, who usually hate you particularly and (in the case of the Hosts and the Claimed) are insults to the memory of Father/Mother Wolf?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I can't tell if you're acting childish as an ironic thing here or if you actually don't understand how distribution of focus operates in a written work. </div> </div> </div>This was more of a joking thing; I am allowed to joke in my for-fun hobby, right?<br /> <hr /><br /> To step back a little:<br /> <br /> I did not personally like the execution of the Idigam. I am aware that people <i>do</i> like them, and therefore they are not all bad... but they are not to my taste.<br /> <br /> Therefore, I will jokingly make posts like the above which essentially go &quot;hey, if you took out the stuff I don't like, you'd <i>totally</i> have space for the stuff I do like! It's like a win-win, except I', the only one who wins, because I'm a selfish asshole&quot;. This is just human nature.<br /> <br /> But would I have preferred to see Bale Hounds in the book? Not particularly, no.<br /> <br /> I would have preferred having more examples of Claimed and Hosts, since they are more interesting to me, and they feel like they got a very small portion of wordcount (the Pure are really just Werewolves with a different ideology, Spirits get a good number of examples, and Mortals kinda don't need lengthy writeups because it's assumed that we're familiar with them; Claimed and Hosts could do with a little more detail, especially if (like me) this is pretty much your first time picking up Werewolf.)<br /> <br /> If I ruffled any feathers or inadvertently insulted anyone, I apologize. I hope we can all still be friends (angry friends, at the very least.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T15:12:10-07:00","id":436323,"title":"","content":"'Werewolf is a game about the thrill of the hunt, and the fear of being hunted.'<br /> <br /> It's not all about being the big bad wolf, because there's always going to be something out there tougher, meaner, badder and better than you are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":".  Added quotes, sort of, because it's a quotation. 03-10-2015, 06:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T15:30:56-07:00","id":436345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/431772-2ed-bale-hounds?p=436315#post436315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I mentioned in another thread, B&amp;S could get away with that because Strix were one of four things, while the Idigam are trying to be one of eight things (eleven things, if you count the extra stuff that they can make as separate things). Plus, pulling in other gamelines with a very different distribution of &quot;baddies&quot; is kinda... not entirely comparing apples to apples.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then here's a different thing that is the same thing: Remember Devourers from <i>Autumn Nightmares</i>? Remember the Extempore from <i>Magnum Opus</i>? Remember all the weird shit from <i>Night Horrors: Wicked Dead</i>?<br /> <br /> If you don't, that's fine, but that means you're in the same boat as people who only read the corebooks for the first editions of Changeling, Promethean, and Vampire.<br /> <br /> You may also note that the latter two have specifically had parts of their constituent elements included in the 2e corebooks! (The Strix debuted in <i>Requiem for Rome</i>, yes, but <i>Wicked Dead</i> gave them their first modern incarnation.)<br /> <br /> This is not an accident, as it makes those things easy to include without having to comb through several books to find a proper breadth of references. (It's been about two years since my Grand WtF1e Readthrough, but I distinctly remember that idigam hooks were spread across at least three books before <i>Night Horrors: Wolfsbane</i> debuted their actual mechanics <i>four years after the corebook dropped</i>. As the <i>second-to-last traditional-print book of the line.</i>) Take note of the list of 1e books at the front of the 2e core; its inclusion is there in part to help supplement the dearth of information on certain prey in the book itself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Idigam just feel like their own thing, and I'm not sure how I would use them to fuel stories without having one <i>right there</i>. I mean, with Strix or the God-Machine or Angels or whatever, you can play on dread and paranoia and the like; you can bluff that they are coming and make it work. </div> </div> </div><i>Hunting Ground: The Rockies</i> may have premiered early in 1e, but it very specifically covers some of the leftover fallout of an idigam who's been &quot;dead&quot; for an ambiguous period of time, including a pack of <i>su'ur</i> whose totem is basically said idigam's &quot;ghost.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But Werewolf? Werewolf isn't about being <i>afraid</i> of things. It's about a lot of things (the hunt, family, territory, coming to terms with how you changed and are changing), but it isn't about worrying about nebulous threats. You've got that Pure pack next door baring their fangs at you, the Beshilu making trouble down by the docks, and some spirits getting too big for their britches on YOUR territory... so why should you care about some nebulous threat? </div> </div> </div>Because that nebulous threat is fucking up your territory as only a godlike protean monster can.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This was more of a joking thing; I am allowed to joke in my for-fun hobby, right? </div> </div> </div>With due respect, <i>not in the middle of an argument.</i> It gives cause to believe you aren't taking the discussion seriously and are either suffering a terminal lack of understanding about the topic or deliberately trying to rile people, neither of which is something you want a reputation for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T17:30:29-07:00","id":436450,"title":"","content":"Oh, shit, there was an argument?<br /> <br /> Colour me chagrined. I misread the tone of the thread.<br /> <br /> Good day, folks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}